Hi Desire, Junqi, and all,

I'm the lead developer on mcera5 R package, which holds the functions that query ERA5 data and are called from within micro_era5(). The concerns that Desire brings up are valid, and stem partly from how the CDS API is set up, and partly from how mcera5 was written to conform to that API.

The approach Junqi describes, using the ARCO ERA Zarr data is probably the right way forward. This was released a few months ago, and I hope to find the time to update mcera5 to reflect this new archive. But this likely won't happen until November, perhaps Oct at the earliest, given the time needed to test before releasing a new version of the package. If your needs are urgent then I'd follow Junqi's workaround for now. And, the mcera5 software is on GitHub <https://github.com/dklinges9/mcera5> – feel free to submit pull requests if there is a method you have worked on.

Best,
Dave

